    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The documentation requirements for a verbal warning are crucial, just like a goblin's treasure map is essential for finding the loot. You'll want to make sure you're recording the following details:\n\n* The date and time of the verbal warning\n* The specific behavior or performance issue that was discussed\n* The expected improvements or corrective actions\n* The employee's acknowledgment of the issue and their understanding of the expectations\n* Any agreements or next steps discussed during the meeting\n\nIt's also a good idea to have a template or a standard form for verbal warnings, just like a goblin's treasure map has a standard layout. This will help ensure that you're consistently documenting the same information and that it's easily accessible for future reference.\n\nAnd, just like a goblin's treasure map might have a hidden clause or two, you may also want to consider including a clause in the verbal warning that outlines the consequences of not meeting the expected improvements. This will help ensure that the employee understands the gravity of the situation and is more likely to take the necessary steps to correct their behavior.\n\nBy the way, have you ever heard of the \"Goblin's Gambit\" in negotiations? It's a clever tactic where you offer a concession in exchange for a more",
